*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.jpg
*.wav
*.log

# tools/find/FIND.COM is a BUILD ARTIFACT of tools/find/FIND.ASM (assemble
# with `nasm -f bin FIND.ASM -o FIND.COM`, or run build-and-test.sh, which
# rewrites it in place on every run). It predates the "the SOURCE is the
# record" rule below and was tracked before that rule existed; untracked
# and ignored here instead of carrying a second copy that can silently
# disagree with the source that produces it.
/tools/find/FIND.COM

# The operator's real configuration. The tracked example is
# examples/vcctrl.example.yaml.
/vcctrl.yaml
# Any sibling profile -- `vcctrl-<name>.yaml` is a live config vcctrld will
# load as a running profile (discover_profiles() globs exactly this
# pattern). No negation needed here (unlike before the example configs
# moved to examples/): nothing this pattern matches at the repo root is
# ever meant to be tracked.
/vcctrl-*.yaml

# This rig's real capture-device pin (by-id paths, ALSA card id). The
# tracked example is pi/files/device-pin.conf.example.
/pi/files/device-pin.conf

# PLANNING WORK THAT MUST NEVER REACH THE REPOSITORY.
#
# Plans, drafts, scratch analysis, anything written to think with rather than
# to ship. Ignored as a DIRECTORY, deliberately: an untracked single file is
# one `git add -A docs` away from being committed, and that is not
# hypothetical -- docs/CONFIG-PLAN.md was swept into a commit that way during
# the phase-7 rewrite and had to be amended out before the push. A directory
# cannot be caught by a path-scoped add.
#
# It also survives a history scrub without needing an exemption: nothing in
# here is tracked, so nothing in here is in any blob, and a rewrite cannot
# reach it. The cost is the other half of that -- NO BUNDLE CONTAINS IT
# EITHER. Anything here that matters wants a copy outside the tree.
/internal/

# Build artifacts. The SOURCE is the record; the .COM is reproducible from it
# (`make`), and a tracked binary is a second copy that can disagree with it.
/dos/build/

# Claude Code's isolated worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/<name>/` is a full
# registered checkout of this repo -- 3.2 MB of it on 2026-08-25, on its own
# branch, locked, and belonging to whichever session created it.
#
# NOT `/.claude/` wholesale: project-level Claude config that somebody
# deliberately tracks would belong in the repo, and a blanket ignore would
# hide it silently. Only the tooling's scratch checkouts are ignored.
#
# It has shown as `?? .claude/` all day and nothing had swept it, for two
# reasons that are both accidents rather than defences: a registered worktree
# carries a `.git` file, so `add` will not recurse into it -- and the nested
# copy of THIS file is what was ignoring its `internal/`, since `/internal/`
# is root-anchored and does not match a nested one. Neither fact is something
# to rely on. An untracked directory in this tree is a thing waiting to be
# added by somebody who did not look.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The protocol-board firmware build: fetched upstream source + objects. The
# SOURCE of record is fetch.sh's pins plus firmware/usb4vc-ibmpc/patches/.
/firmware/usb4vc-ibmpc/build/
